it repository in /tmp/bare/.git/\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare (git)-[master] % mkdir baresub\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare (git)-[master] % cd baresub\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare/baresub (git)-[master] % git init --bare\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/bare/baresub/\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare/baresub (git)-[master] % cd ..\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare (git)-[master] % git add .\nmih@meiner /tmp/bare (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\n\nNo commits yet\n\nChanges to be committed:\n  (use \"git rm --cached \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n        new file:   baresub/HEAD\n        new file:   baresub/config\n        new file:   baresub/description\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/applypatch-msg.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/commit-msg.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/fsmonitor-watchman.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/post-update.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/pre-applypatch.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/pre-commit.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/pre-push.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/pre-rebase.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/pre-receive.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/prepare-commit-msg.sample\n        new file:   baresub/hooks/update.sample\n        new file:   baresub/info/exclude\n```\n\nWith a .gitignore in place `add` does not add it. Without a .gitignore there is no other functional relationship between the super and the bare .git folder than being tracked file by file, as it cannot become a submodule.","files":null}]}